<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb pork imports fall 21.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb pork imports fall 21.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in February totalled 19,708 tonnes, down 21.4 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Feb 97	Jan 97	 Feb 96</p>
<p> Total	     19,708	33,997	 25,074</p>
<p> Refrigerated    10,490	 9,258	 10,795</p>
<p> Frozen	     9,218	24,739	 14,279</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     4,884	 4,167	  5,360</p>
<p> U.S.		 4,769	 4,234	  4,817</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Feb 97	Jan 97	 Feb 96</p>
<p> Taiwan	     3,907	11,838	 10,276</p>
<p>Total imports of refrigerated pork in the first two months of calendar 1997 totalled 19,883 tonnes against 19,255 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Total imports of frozen pork in the January-February period of this year totalled 33,956 tonnes against 27,541 tonnes a year earlier, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
